{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "כבד את אביך", :translit "kabeid et avikha", :gloss "Honor your father"} {:he "שבת", :translit "shabbat", :gloss "Sabbath"} {:he "וכבדתו", :translit "vekibadto", :gloss "and you shall honor it"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (semikhut) of the father-honor commandment to the Sabbath commandment"}], :frame {:text "The verse וכבדת את השבת from Isaiah 58:13 establishes that the Sabbath must be honored, and Shabbat 118a specifies that this means honoring it with special food and clean garments. The verbal link between כבד (honor) for parents and כבד for Sabbath teaches that parental honor likewise involves food and clothing.", :sources ["Isaiah 58:13" "Shabbat 118a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ולמען ייטב לך", :translit "ulema'an yitav lakh", :gloss "and that it may go well with you"} {:he "תגין על הטי\"ת", :translit "tagin al ha-tet", :gloss "tagin on the tet"} {:he "ט' חדשים", :translit "tet chodashim", :gloss "nine months"} {:he "ט' מדות", :translit "tet midot", :gloss "nine traits"} {:he "אסנ\"ת משגע\"ח", :translit "ASNAT MSGaKH", :gloss "acronym-mnemonic for the nine traits"} {:he "בני אנוסה", :translit "banei anusa", :gloss "children of a forced woman"} {:he "בני שנואה", :translit "banei senu'a", :gloss "children of a hated woman"} {:he "בני נדה", :translit "banei nida", :gloss "children of a menstruant"} {:he "בני תמורה", :translit "banei temura", :gloss "children of substitution"} {:he "בני מריבה", :translit "banei meriva", :gloss "children of strife"} {:he "בני שכרות", :translit "banei shikhrut", :gloss "children of drunkenness"} {:he "בני גרושת הלב", :translit "banei gerushat halev", :gloss "children of heart-divorced"} {:he "בני ערבוביא", :translit "banei arvuvya", :gloss "children of mixture"} {:he "בני חצופה", :translit "banei chatsufa", :gloss "children of a brazen woman"} {:he "טוב", :translit "tov", :gloss "good"} {:he "י\"ז תיבות יתרות דברות אחרונות על הראשונות", :translit "yud-zayin teivot